From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:13:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: reconcile TC4 credits before a sequence recycle

On station 9 the recycle at the tenth lifetime was refused with TC4 at
23 of 26 pages, nothing pending and TC1 complete: the cleanup's last
command pages had not been reconciled yet. An ordinary re-arm never
meets this, because the next scan's guard reconciles the credits
before its first command; the recycle checks the ledger before that.

Reconcile first, as the scan guard does, and while TC4 is still short
wait for it, up to 25 re-arm passes 20 ms apart, before the old wrap
refusal. The recycle line now reports the passes waited.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
index 8bfd0e16c..e2c019f5b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
@@ -244,6 +244,8 @@ struct mt6797_mac {
 	unsigned int sequence;
 	/* The first command sequence of lifetime 1, where a recycle restarts. */
 	unsigned int sequence_base;
+	/* Re-arm passes a recycle has waited for TC4 credits, at most 25. */
+	unsigned int join_recycle_waits;
 	bool configured, closing;
 	int first_error;
 	bool join_deauth_status_valid, join_deauth_status_late;
@@ -4792,10 +4794,31 @@ static void mt6797_mac_join_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			mt6797_mac_join_rearm(mac);
 			break;
 		case MT6797_JOIN_REARM_RECYCLE:
+			{
+				struct mt6797_hif_tx_status status;
+				struct mt6797_normal_release account;
+
+				/* The cleanup's last command pages may not be reconciled
+				 * yet; the next scan's guard would reconcile them before
+				 * its command, so do the same here. While TC4 is still
+				 * short, wait for it: 25 passes 20 ms apart.
+				 */
+				mt6797_hif_reconcile_runtime(mac->hif,
+							     ktime_get_ns() + 20 * NSEC_PER_MSEC,
+							     &status, &account);
+			}
 			recycled = mt6797_hif_recycle_sequences(mac->hif, mac->sequence_base);
+			if (recycled == -EBUSY && mac->join_recycle_waits < 25) {
+				mac->join_recycle_waits++;
+				mac->join_rearm_pending = true;
+				schedule_delayed_work(&mac->join_work, msecs_to_jiffies(20));
+				break;
+			}
 			dev_info(wiphy_dev(mac->hw->wiphy),
-				 "one-shot WLAN join rearm sequence recycle: from=%u to=%u ret=%d\n",
-				 mac->sequence, mac->sequence_base, recycled);
+				 "one-shot WLAN join rearm sequence recycle: from=%u to=%u ret=%d waits=%u\n",
+				 mac->sequence, mac->sequence_base, recycled,
+				 mac->join_recycle_waits);
+			mac->join_recycle_waits = 0;
 			if (!recycled) {
 				mac->sequence = mac->sequence_base;
 				mt6797_mac_join_rearm(mac);
-- 
2.43.0

